<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adham Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1531–1562</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adham Khan was a Mughal general, son of the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar</a>'s wet-nurse Maham Anga. In 1561 he defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baz-bahadur">Baz Bahadur</a>, the last sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a>, at Sarangpur, but his cruelty and seizure of the spoils angered Akbar. In 1562 he murdered the minister Ataga Khan in the palace, and Akbar had him thrown twice from a terrace to his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/adham-khan.jpg" alt="Adham Khan" width="320" height="499" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: La'l, Sanwala · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marriage_of_Adham_Khan,_son_of_Mahan_Anga,_Akbarnama.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
